    "case_id": "615",
    "case_summary": "A 52-year-old Caucasian man presented with septic shock and bilateral lower extremity soft-tissue wounds. Medical history includes alcohol use disorder and newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (hemoglobin A1c of 7.5%). The patient had no history or findings suggestive of cirrhosis and had not traveled outside Southern California.\n\nPatient presented with bilateral lower extremity soft-tissue wounds. Additional physical examination details were not provided in the case report.\n\n- Laboratory Tests:    * Blood and wound cultures grew Klebsiella pneumoniae    * Microbiology showed positive string test    * Organism showed resistance only to ampicillin    - Imaging Studies:    * Initial MRI: Showed left mid-tibia osteomyelitis with an adjacent abscess and right third toe osteomyelitis    * Abdominal Ultrasound: Revealed an 8.4 × 11 × 13 cm liver abscess    * Bone Scan: Showed increased uptake in the right humerus and bilateral femurs    * Follow-up MRI: Confirmed osteomyelitis in right humerus and bilateral femurs    - Pathological Tests:    * Right femur biopsy: Demonstrated abscess formation",
